W3C Verifiable Credentials Data Integrity JSON-LD contexts

Sources and copies (byte for byte, as served with
Accept: application/ld+json):
  - https://w3id.org/security/data-integrity/v2 -> data-integrity-v2.jsonld
    (redirects to https://www.w3.org/2025/credentials/vcdi/context/v2.jsonld)
  - https://w3id.org/security/multikey/v1 -> multikey-v1.jsonld
    (redirects to
    https://www.w3.org/2025/credentials/vcdi/multikey/context/v1.jsonld)

Neither file carries a copyright or licence notice of its own.

Both contexts, with the SHA-256 digests recorded in pin.json, are listed in
the W3C Recommendation "Verifiable Credential Data Integrity 1.0",
https://www.w3.org/TR/vc-data-integrity/, published by the Verifiable
Credentials Working Group. It carries this notice: "Copyright © 2025 World
Wide Web Consortium. W3C® liability, trademark and permissive document
license rules apply." Its permissive document license link is
